#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# sinh_integral

#% text
# `sinh_integral(x)` gives the hyperbolic sine integral `Shi(x)`, the integral of `sinh(t)/t` for `t` from 0 to `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The definition is DLMF 6.2.15. `Shi` is odd and entire.

#% item
# `sinh_integral(0)` is 0. Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% item
# `sinh_integral` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
sinh_integral(1.0)
#% output
#= 1.0572508753757286

#% cell
sinh_integral(0)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
sinh_integral(-3.0)
#% output
#= -4.973440475859807

#% cell
n(sinh_integral(1), 30)
#% output
#= 1.0572508753757285145718423548958780

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The derivative:

#% cell
d(sinh_integral(x), x)
#% output
#= sinh(x)/x

#% text
# `Shi` is the mean of the two exponential integrals:

#% cell
sinh_integral(2.0) - (exp_integral_ei(2.0) + exp_integral_e(1, 2.0))/2
#% output
#= 0.0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `cosh_integral`, `sin_integral`, `exp_integral_ei`
